# Loop goal-refinement — the honest-refuse terminal becomes a bounded refinement entry + the milestone-leg seam

The owner product steer (Luke, Telegram 11408; binding foundation,
NOT re-litigated) ruled the correct behaviour at the loop's
give-up point is neither fake nor refuse — it is REFINE: a non-tech
user must accomplish what they want with AI; an unmeasurable goal
is refined toward measurable (interactive-refine first, else
self-refine); and when the real goal is not directly measurable at
all, pick a measurable milestone ON THE PATH, get explicit
agreement, achieve it, then check in. This amendment converts the
sealed intake's two dead-ends into entries into a BOUNDED
refinement construct — a CONTAINED EVOLUTION of the intake
derivation, NOT a loop re-architecture (decompose/dispatch/judge
UNTOUCHED, AC.FOUND.0) + ONE named in-scope prerequisite (the
intake->loop seam, milestone-leg-only).

